# p08 bounded value: two sourced figures that disagree
#
# LinkML option: none (docs/crosswalk.md, cause d: a bounded value, not a missing one).
#
# Two figures from the English Wikipedia article "Napoleon complex" (read 2026-09-14): about
# 1.67 m (5 feet 2 inches in French measures) and 1.70 m (5 feet 7 inches, given by other
# historians). The datum's value specification carries no point value. It is typed with an OWL
# datatype restriction: it has some numeric value between 1.67 and 1.70 inclusive. The two
# figures are kept as their own value specifications, linked with BFO:0000051 'has part' (a choice
# made for this example, not an OBI pattern, as in the template).
#
# The interval is this record's summary of two disagreeing estimates. It is not a claim that the
# true height lies between them.
#
# OBI gaps (template p08, checked 2026-09-14): no 'less than' relation, no range value
# specification class, no minimum or maximum numeric value properties outside age.
#
# A consumer can infer a stated range and where each end came from. A plain SPARQL consumer has
# to read the restriction structure; an OWL reasoner treats it as a real constraint.

@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/napoleon/> .
@prefix BFO:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_> .
@prefix IAO:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_> .
@prefix OBI:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_> .
@prefix UO:   <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_> .

ex:heightAssay1 a owl:NamedIndividual , OBI:0003817 ;
    BFO:0000050 ex:examination1 ;
    OBI:0000293 ex:napoleon ;
    OBI:0000299 ex:heightDatum1 .

ex:heightDatum1 a owl:NamedIndividual , IAO:0000109 ;
    IAO:0000136 ex:napoleonHeight ;
    OBI:0001938 ex:valueSpec1 ;
    BFO:0000051 ex:estimate1 , ex:estimate2 .

ex:valueSpec1 a owl:NamedIndividual , OBI:0001931 ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty OBI:0001937 ;
          owl:someValuesFrom
            [ a rdfs:Datatype ;
              owl:onDatatype xsd:decimal ;
              owl:withRestrictions ( [ xsd:minInclusive "1.67"^^xsd:decimal ]
                                     [ xsd:maxInclusive "1.70"^^xsd:decimal ] ) ] ] ;
    IAO:0000039 UO:0000008 .

ex:estimate1 a owl:NamedIndividual , OBI:0001931 ;
    rdfs:comment "5 feet 2 inches in pre-metric French measures, about 1.67 m (Wikipedia, Napoleon complex, read 2026-09-14)" ;
    OBI:0001937 "1.67"^^xsd:decimal ;
    IAO:0000039 UO:0000008 .

ex:estimate2 a owl:NamedIndividual , OBI:0001931 ;
    rdfs:comment "5 feet 7 inches (1.70 m), given by other historians (Wikipedia, Napoleon complex, read 2026-09-14)" ;
    OBI:0001937 "1.70"^^xsd:decimal ;
    IAO:0000039 UO:0000008 .
